WEBVTT

00:01.010 --> 00:06.680
<i>Fushi borrows Funa's form 
in an attempt to save Mizuha.</i>

00:07.060 --> 00:10.860
And your idea was to throw 
these things around?

00:11.150 --> 00:13.190
I was using it.

00:13.620 --> 00:15.610
And I won.

00:16.410 --> 00:20.760
<i>Fushi returns home to his friends.</i>

00:22.040 --> 00:28.480
I don't think they're happy.

02:00.010 --> 02:04.010
Where One Belongs

02:33.580 --> 02:35.090
Ow...

02:35.090 --> 02:36.850
Hey, Gugu?

02:36.850 --> 02:37.920
This wound?

02:37.920 --> 02:40.130
I did that "plastic surgery" thing.

02:40.420 --> 02:42.850
Your mask was broken.

02:42.850 --> 02:45.530
Oh, I fell down the stairs.

02:45.530 --> 02:47.190
My clothes got completely torn up.

02:47.190 --> 02:48.730
Hairo fell with me, too.

02:50.190 --> 02:52.020
Gross!

02:52.020 --> 02:53.430
Are you bleeding?!

02:53.740 --> 02:55.660
Did you get a cut in your mouth?

02:55.660 --> 02:57.870
Your dentures broke when 
you fell with me, right?

02:57.870 --> 03:00.070
Something must have happened, right, Gugu?

03:01.200 --> 03:03.730
Are you all right? Can you eat okay?

03:05.020 --> 03:07.800
Sorry for making you worry.

03:07.800 --> 03:11.750
I was out on some errands, and Gramps 
and Aiko both happened to be out, too.

03:11.750 --> 03:13.460
No, uh...

03:13.710 --> 03:16.580
I'm just glad you're back.

03:16.580 --> 03:18.170
I should let Bon-san know.

03:19.100 --> 03:20.510
Where is Bon?

03:20.510 --> 03:23.130
He's out of town. 
Overseas business trip, apparently.

03:23.770 --> 03:26.300
Oh, Fushi, you're back.

03:26.300 --> 03:27.220
Messar.

03:27.220 --> 03:29.750
How did everyone end up like this?

03:29.750 --> 03:32.220
Huh? They're all fine.

03:32.220 --> 03:33.060
But...

03:33.350 --> 03:37.520
Does it look like they've changed 
while you'd run away from home?

03:39.040 --> 03:42.190
They aren't used to this world 
that they got whisked away to.

03:42.190 --> 03:44.540
They're trying to live their lives here.

03:44.540 --> 03:45.710
That's all.

03:45.710 --> 03:48.800
That's it? That's why they're so down?

03:48.800 --> 03:51.660
No one's dead. They're doing 
better than they were before.

03:51.970 --> 03:54.500
Not that I'm fazed at all.

03:54.500 --> 03:57.140
True, you haven't changed at all.

03:57.710 --> 03:59.740
Because I'm clear-eyed.

03:59.740 --> 04:02.060
Take a good look at your buddies.

04:14.330 --> 04:18.090
Gugu, I just made this.

04:18.090 --> 04:19.970
Ooh, thanks.

04:20.340 --> 04:21.860
Sorry if it isn't quite right.

04:21.860 --> 04:23.410
About your injury...

04:23.410 --> 04:26.080
I think you were lying about falling.

04:26.620 --> 04:27.910
Ow!

04:28.200 --> 04:30.230
It kinda rubs against my wound.

04:30.230 --> 04:31.480
Sorry.

04:31.480 --> 04:33.460
How about this one?

04:33.460 --> 04:34.880
It's really fluffy.

04:34.880 --> 04:37.310
What's up with this weird-ass thing?

04:37.890 --> 04:40.560
It's the crayfish mask Rean made.

04:40.560 --> 04:42.010
Takes you back, doesn't it?

04:43.050 --> 04:44.230
Rean made it?!

04:44.230 --> 04:44.890
Yeah.

04:45.170 --> 04:47.000
I just called it weird-ass!

04:47.000 --> 04:48.690
Rean made this?

04:48.690 --> 04:50.280
For me?!

04:51.340 --> 04:52.900
Oh, right.

04:53.310 --> 04:56.050
She never had a chance to give it to you.

04:58.530 --> 04:59.460
How's it look?

04:59.460 --> 05:00.740
Good, good.

05:01.040 --> 05:02.400
Yeah?

05:02.400 --> 05:03.940
Rean made it, huh?

05:04.170 --> 05:05.060
Yeah.

05:06.450 --> 05:09.110
Man, I want to go back to Takunaha.

05:12.380 --> 05:14.260
Are you serious?

05:14.260 --> 05:15.330
Wh-Why?

05:15.330 --> 05:17.630
Did you not like Yanome?

05:17.630 --> 05:19.110
That's not it.

05:19.590 --> 05:22.800
You brought me back to life 
in Takunaha, remember?

05:29.040 --> 05:31.800
Booze Man's shop was still around.

05:32.490 --> 05:35.330
It brought back some memories.

05:36.470 --> 05:38.900
I'm just kidding, though.

05:39.510 --> 05:40.510
Night.

05:55.720 --> 05:59.710
<i>Maybe this wasn't a good place for them.</i>

05:59.710 --> 06:02.760
Fushi, I got a message from Bon-san.

06:02.760 --> 06:04.460
He says to look at this.

06:05.060 --> 06:08.780
The International Weeding Federation 
says they're going to get rid

06:08.780 --> 06:11.210
of all the roots you've spread 
over the past 500 years.

06:11.210 --> 06:14.060
<i>The roots in Renril have stopped growing.</i>

06:14.060 --> 06:16.620
<i>Now's our chance to finally 
do away with them.</i>

06:16.620 --> 06:19.420
<i>No, the great tree is still alive.</i>

06:17.480 --> 06:18.910
Oh, it's Bon.

06:19.420 --> 06:21.570
<i>I see you're a Fushi fundamentalist.</i>

06:21.570 --> 06:23.440
<i>You're as silly as the roots.</i>

06:23.440 --> 06:25.220
<i>Your ideology is a curse.</i>

06:25.220 --> 06:27.400
I'm not a curse!

06:27.400 --> 06:29.100
There's more I can do!

06:30.080 --> 06:32.320
<i>The idea that the roots have stopped growing</i>

06:32.320 --> 06:34.980
<i>is a lie spread by the Church of Bennett.</i>

06:36.510 --> 06:37.760
Yes!

06:37.760 --> 06:38.870
That's right.

06:39.240 --> 06:40.780
I can keep going!

07:04.110 --> 07:05.600
Welcome.

07:06.400 --> 07:08.230
I'm working right now.

07:09.200 --> 07:13.880
I came to ask if something 
happened to you and Gugu.

07:13.880 --> 07:16.160
Like he said, we fell.

07:16.160 --> 07:19.010
By the way, do you have enough dentures?

07:19.010 --> 07:21.480
Yes, I have the ones from before.

07:21.870 --> 07:24.590
You don't need the newest ones?

07:28.610 --> 07:33.970
Gugu's never been able to fit in at school.

07:34.720 --> 07:36.530
What's up with the mask?

07:36.530 --> 07:38.390
I have an injury.

07:38.390 --> 07:39.470
Let's see.

07:39.820 --> 07:42.490
Come on! Lemme see.

07:44.510 --> 07:47.100
For better or worse, 
people were fascinated by him.

07:47.100 --> 07:49.780
He struggled with all the people 
following him around every day.

07:50.340 --> 07:53.310
Too bad we aren't in the same grade.

07:53.310 --> 07:56.280
Maybe they'll be satisfied if I show them.

07:58.500 --> 08:00.880
Kinda normal... I guess?

08:00.880 --> 08:03.640
Hey! Stop bullying the new kid.

08:03.640 --> 08:05.250
I'm not, Sensei.

08:05.250 --> 08:07.590
I was just fascinated by his mask.

08:07.590 --> 08:10.970
But the rumor spread further
and brought even more trouble.

08:07.590 --> 08:13.430
The hell's with your bird mask, kid?

08:13.430 --> 08:16.940
Acchan runs the show around these parts.

08:16.940 --> 08:20.720
You've got some nerve wandering around 
without so much as saying hi!

08:20.720 --> 08:22.240
Who's Acchan?

08:22.240 --> 08:24.010
You being smart with me?!

08:24.780 --> 08:26.320
Ow!

08:26.320 --> 08:28.700
This guy's bad news, Acchan!

08:28.700 --> 08:31.190
You've gone and done it now.

08:31.190 --> 08:33.450
Dude, I haven't done anything.

08:33.450 --> 08:36.940
You trying to be the town 
mascot or something?

08:38.400 --> 08:40.270
You! Stop!

08:40.270 --> 08:41.090
What was that?

08:41.090 --> 08:43.330
It's cracked!

08:43.330 --> 08:46.080
Look what you've done to my mask!

08:46.080 --> 08:47.960
Apologize!

08:47.960 --> 08:49.340
Relax, Gugu!

08:49.340 --> 08:51.120
You're going to cause trouble for Kazumitsu!

08:51.120 --> 08:52.620
Take that!

08:53.250 --> 08:55.090
Are you serious?

08:55.090 --> 08:56.430
It didn't do anything!

08:56.430 --> 08:57.460
Why?!

09:02.340 --> 09:03.890
All right...

09:03.890 --> 09:05.900
I guess I'm getting involved.

09:05.900 --> 09:06.930
Thanks.

09:17.140 --> 09:19.310
That went on for days.

09:19.310 --> 09:22.240
Eventually, we were captured 
by people in blue.

09:23.050 --> 09:25.450
That's the story up to yesterday.

09:25.450 --> 09:29.000
Gugu said he wanted to go back to Takunaha.

09:29.320 --> 09:31.900
It's a good place for sure.

09:31.900 --> 09:32.590
But...

09:35.010 --> 09:39.250
Is it not nice living here?

09:39.520 --> 09:41.340
I'm not sure.

09:41.340 --> 09:44.370
Either way, I'll be leaving 
that home within a year.

09:46.140 --> 09:47.390
Why?!

09:47.390 --> 09:49.860
There's a place to sleep 
and the food is good.

09:50.140 --> 09:54.580
I can't keep acting like a kid forever.

09:54.580 --> 09:58.700
If you think about how many years I've lived, 
I'm older than Kazumitsu.

09:58.700 --> 10:00.560
I don't get it.

10:00.560 --> 10:02.450
Is that place not good enough?

10:02.650 --> 10:04.050
What's wrong with it?

10:04.050 --> 10:04.920
School?

10:04.920 --> 10:06.010
Or me?

10:06.010 --> 10:07.490
Calm down. Please.

10:07.490 --> 10:09.400
I'm not leaving because I hate it.

10:09.880 --> 10:13.380
This world you've brought us to is so fun.

10:13.380 --> 10:16.120
I just want to go explore some more.

10:22.240 --> 10:23.680
Where are you going?!

10:24.050 --> 10:26.180
<i>I can do more.</i>

10:31.010 --> 10:33.800
You're serious about wanting to 
go back to Takunaha, aren't you?

10:34.540 --> 10:38.980
Do you seriously think Fushi's 
going to see you off with a smile?

10:39.250 --> 10:41.940
I'm sure he already knows.

10:42.560 --> 10:46.340
I didn't want him to see me 
messed up after the fights.

10:46.340 --> 10:48.450
I can't believe he'd come 
home out of nowhere.

10:48.450 --> 10:49.850
Damn it, Fushi...

10:50.270 --> 10:52.780
Just tell him everything 
that's pissing you off.

10:52.780 --> 10:55.660
I don't want to be <i>that</i> brother.

10:55.660 --> 10:56.910
You sure?

10:56.910 --> 10:59.490
That's what I would prefer, if anything.

11:01.740 --> 11:05.630
A big brother ought to understand 
his kid brother better.

11:06.080 --> 11:08.470
Is Fushi-san not home?

11:08.470 --> 11:09.980
He's not here.

11:10.280 --> 11:14.030
I told him about our injuries, and he ran off.

11:14.460 --> 11:16.200
I thought he'd be here.

11:18.600 --> 11:21.740
It's just us and the animals here right now.

11:21.740 --> 11:24.840
Can anyone help me find Fushi?

11:26.000 --> 11:27.870
Okay, you.

11:28.780 --> 11:31.660
They understand words?

11:32.540 --> 11:34.290
I'm gonna go get Fushi.

11:38.880 --> 11:41.280
Is he really here?

11:41.280 --> 11:43.590
It's another fight.

11:43.590 --> 11:45.340
That masked guy again?

11:45.340 --> 11:46.670
Sheesh.

11:50.200 --> 11:51.510
Why are you—

11:51.510 --> 11:53.110
Ow, ow, ow!

11:53.600 --> 11:54.790
Hey!

11:54.790 --> 11:56.350
You're Fushi, aren't you?

11:56.350 --> 11:58.330
What are you doing? Stop!

11:58.330 --> 12:00.240
Gugu?! Why are you here?

12:00.240 --> 12:01.890
What are you yapping about?

12:01.890 --> 12:02.730
Move!

12:02.730 --> 12:04.870
Run! This way!

12:04.870 --> 12:07.260
Hold up, asshole!

12:09.200 --> 12:13.260
What the hell are you doing wearing my mask?

12:15.100 --> 12:16.520
Sorry.

12:16.520 --> 12:19.070
I know that face...

12:19.070 --> 12:20.120
Nando!

12:20.120 --> 12:20.930
Yeah.

12:20.930 --> 12:21.780
I knew it.

12:21.780 --> 12:22.950
Why Nando?

12:22.950 --> 12:26.090
His body's the closest to yours.

12:26.090 --> 12:27.560
What kind of reason is that?

12:27.970 --> 12:31.410
I wanted to know how you've 
been living your life.

12:31.410 --> 12:35.780
I asked around in town, 
and those guys jumped me.

12:37.220 --> 12:41.260
I hate anyone who hurts you.

12:41.260 --> 12:42.680
I couldn't hold myself back.

12:43.320 --> 12:44.700
Sorry, Gugu.

12:44.700 --> 12:47.100
I've been putting you through so much pain.

12:47.100 --> 12:48.720
I had no idea.

12:48.720 --> 12:50.200
I get it.

12:50.730 --> 12:55.060
You've been tilling soil for us potatoes.

12:55.060 --> 12:56.200
Potatoes?

12:56.620 --> 12:58.060
Never mind.

13:06.100 --> 13:08.930
Takunaha's better than here.

13:09.330 --> 13:10.520
Yeah.

13:11.060 --> 13:14.890
Booze Man's shop had barely changed.

13:15.600 --> 13:17.950
I was staring at it in awe, and...

13:20.140 --> 13:21.250
Hello.

13:21.600 --> 13:25.110
The guy at the shop looked 
just like my brother.

13:26.100 --> 13:29.990
I realized my brother had protected it.

13:34.320 --> 13:35.900
H-Hey.

13:36.680 --> 13:41.760
I... My name is Gugu. I'm a servant here.

13:41.760 --> 13:43.110
Listen up, Fushi.

13:43.110 --> 13:48.430
Since you're going to be living here, 
you need to learn the work.

13:49.270 --> 13:52.000
I'll work here, too.

14:34.360 --> 14:36.770
So it's just like it was back then.

14:37.990 --> 14:39.060
Yeah.

14:39.630 --> 14:41.180
That mask...

14:41.910 --> 14:44.130
Oh, this? It's tacky, huh?

14:44.130 --> 14:45.380
I just bought it earlier.

14:45.380 --> 14:47.260
Nah, it looks great.

14:47.260 --> 14:49.030
It's the festival tomorrow, after all.

14:49.360 --> 14:51.180
Please come in.

15:05.170 --> 15:08.090
That's Rean Cropp.

15:08.090 --> 15:10.750
She used to run this shop.

15:11.070 --> 15:14.930
Supposedly, she never got married. 
She was waiting for her love to return to her.

15:15.670 --> 15:19.320
My ancestor had that picture 
made a long time ago.

15:19.710 --> 15:21.020
Your ancestor?

15:22.680 --> 15:23.590
Here.

15:23.590 --> 15:25.470
This is the brewery as it was before.

15:25.470 --> 15:27.440
It hasn't changed much, huh?

15:29.080 --> 15:31.260
This man's my ancestor.

15:31.260 --> 15:33.160
The one in the middle is the founder.

15:33.620 --> 15:36.120
And this is Rean Cropp.

15:37.110 --> 15:38.280
And...

15:38.900 --> 15:40.130
Here you are.

15:40.780 --> 15:42.860
Welcome home, Gugu.

15:44.530 --> 15:45.570
Just kidding.

15:45.850 --> 15:48.490
That's an impressive mask.

15:48.490 --> 15:50.240
You have the same figure, too.

15:50.240 --> 15:52.420
You'll be popular at the festival.

15:54.420 --> 15:56.870
Right! The festival!

15:56.870 --> 15:58.590
I've been so excited for it!

15:58.590 --> 15:59.520
Of course.

15:59.520 --> 16:01.570
You should come by tomorrow, 
too, if you'd like.

16:19.830 --> 16:21.360
So I have a grandkid now.

16:20.470 --> 16:21.640
Oh, my.

16:21.640 --> 16:23.500
I wouldn't mind having another one.

16:22.710 --> 16:25.480
What was this festival about again?

16:25.480 --> 16:28.650
What, you're in that outfit, 
and you still don't know?

16:28.650 --> 16:30.330
Are you a tourist?

16:30.330 --> 16:32.130
Yeah... kinda.

16:32.380 --> 16:35.210
It's for Gugu the Beast.

16:35.210 --> 16:36.350
Beast?

16:36.690 --> 16:39.590
In the legends, this is the 
land where he was born.

16:40.140 --> 16:44.300
Long ago, Takunaha was attacked by monsters.

16:44.750 --> 16:48.200
The fire-breathing beast, 
Gugu, defeated all of them.

16:48.500 --> 16:52.720
So we remember him every year.

16:52.720 --> 16:55.030
Look, it's Gugu!

16:55.370 --> 16:56.910
Gugu!

16:57.690 --> 17:00.620
No one would hurt me.

17:01.080 --> 17:03.350
They all welcomed me.

17:04.600 --> 17:10.520
It was like Nii-chan, Rean, and
Booze Man left it all behind as a gift to me.

17:11.850 --> 17:15.970
My memories in Takunaha hadn't ended yet.

17:15.970 --> 17:17.650
They're still going.

17:17.650 --> 17:21.060
My brother, my family, my home, my life...

17:21.490 --> 17:23.680
I could see all of it happening there.

17:25.290 --> 17:29.210
But I'm not going to leave 
behind my kid brother.

17:29.210 --> 17:31.070
And I have no intention of hurting you.

17:32.170 --> 17:33.610
Relax.

17:33.610 --> 17:38.720
No matter how many shitty people there 
are here, I'm not going to Takunaha.

17:42.280 --> 17:44.410
What's up with that face?

17:44.410 --> 17:46.340
Did I say something stupid?

17:46.340 --> 17:49.750
Sorry I'm a weak brother for getting 
all emotional about Takunaha.

17:50.370 --> 17:51.800
That's not it.

17:51.800 --> 17:54.850
I just realized I need to do more.

17:57.140 --> 17:58.370
Look, Fushi.

17:58.860 --> 18:00.120
That's a weird dog.

18:08.340 --> 18:09.820
All right.

18:09.820 --> 18:12.070
I gotta get my shit together, too!

18:23.250 --> 18:24.220
Morning.

18:24.500 --> 18:25.240
Morning.

18:25.660 --> 18:27.400
Take your seats.

18:28.240 --> 18:31.210
I guess no one else is absent 
except Mizuha, with a cold.

18:31.570 --> 18:33.180
Fushi-kun!

18:33.180 --> 18:35.040
You made it to school. Good for you.

18:35.040 --> 18:38.100
I'll have you take the final exam later.

18:44.200 --> 18:46.810
Gugu might be going back to Takunaha.

18:46.810 --> 18:49.010
Hairo said he'll be leaving 
home eventually, too.

18:49.350 --> 18:50.480
What about you?

18:50.890 --> 18:52.360
Are you leaving, too, Tonari?

18:53.310 --> 18:55.980
I haven't made any plans yet.

18:58.710 --> 19:00.120
Are you studying for something?

19:00.120 --> 19:03.030
No. I'm just reading because 
it caught my interest.

19:03.030 --> 19:06.330
I love how there are so many books here.

19:06.330 --> 19:09.790
I might end up leaving if 
I find something interesting.

19:12.740 --> 19:15.360
It seems like everyone's having 
a hard time living here.

19:15.360 --> 19:20.140
No one would have thought of leaving 
if I'd made this place better.

19:21.350 --> 19:23.140
You might be right.

19:23.140 --> 19:25.250
So that's why you're so anxious.

19:27.210 --> 19:30.110
No matter how much of a 
paradise you make this place,

19:30.110 --> 19:32.990
you aren't getting rid of 
people's troubles or anguish.

19:32.990 --> 19:35.170
We're all human, after all.

19:35.610 --> 19:40.530
I see. You'd prefer a world without 
suffering, like the Nokkers do.

19:40.530 --> 19:42.890
N-No way!

19:42.890 --> 19:44.620
I'm not like the Nokkers!

19:44.920 --> 19:47.900
I just want to grant everyone's dreams.

19:47.900 --> 19:50.490
And that's... And yet...

19:50.490 --> 19:52.240
We'll make them come true on our own.

19:53.190 --> 19:57.710
Anyone chasing a dream has to deal with 
setbacks and suffering all the time.

19:57.710 --> 20:01.010
You're suffering because you're 
trying to grant all of our dreams.

20:01.010 --> 20:02.460
We're all in the same boat.

20:03.330 --> 20:09.720
You gave me a young body, but it came 
with all the problems you'd expect.

20:10.010 --> 20:11.540
It's all such a pain.

20:11.540 --> 20:14.160
Can I solve those problems for you?

20:15.170 --> 20:16.870
Maybe you can.

20:16.870 --> 20:18.070
But I'm not telling you.

20:18.390 --> 20:20.380
These problems are all mine.

20:20.380 --> 20:22.770
They're precious to me. 
I want to keep them to myself.

20:23.090 --> 20:25.120
My third life is quick.

20:25.120 --> 20:27.230
The days go by fast.

20:27.230 --> 20:31.250
The same goes for all of us.
We're all looking for our own lives.

20:31.250 --> 20:34.120
But you don't need to be in such a hurry!

20:34.120 --> 20:36.680
I can keep you alive forever.

20:38.270 --> 20:40.960
Aren't you interested in everyone's lives?

20:41.740 --> 20:46.260
Have you ever considered how they 
felt as they died, or how they plan

20:46.260 --> 20:47.920
to live from now on?

20:47.920 --> 20:49.930
S-Sure.

20:50.190 --> 20:51.380
You have?

20:51.380 --> 20:53.080
Well, that's good.

21:00.850 --> 21:02.330
Ten more minutes.

21:10.540 --> 21:12.000
Shoot...

21:12.000 --> 21:16.700
See? I told you you shouldn't work 
until your other arm's better!

21:16.700 --> 21:18.060
I'm sorry.

21:33.170 --> 21:35.020
